## Write 1/x as a power of x
g(x) &= x^2 - \frac{1}{x}
&= x^2 - x^{-1}
## Differentiate each term
Use $\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^n) = nx^{n-1}$ on each term.
g'(x) &= 2x - (-1)x^{-2}
&= 2x + x^{-2}
&= 2x + \frac{1}{x^2}
ANSWER: g'(x) = 2x + \frac{1}{x^2}

## Substitute t = 2.5
\text{Amount} &= 15(0.6)^{2.5}
&= 4.1828\ldots
&\approx 4.18
ANSWER: 4.18 \text{ mg}

## Set the amount equal to 1 and isolate the power
15(0.6)^t &= 1
(0.6)^t &= \frac{1}{15}
## Take logs of both sides
\ln\left(0.6^t\right) &= \ln\frac{1}{15}
Bring the power down in front: $\ln(a^t) = t\ln a$.
t\ln 0.6 &= \ln\frac{1}{15}
## Solve for t
t &= \frac{\ln\frac{1}{15}}{\ln 0.6}
t &= 5.3013\ldots
t &\approx 5.3
ANSWER: t \approx 5.3 \text{ days}

## Recognise a geometric series
The terms are $15 + 15(0.6) + \dots + 15(0.6)^9$: first term $a = 15$, common ratio $r = 0.6$, and $n = 10$ terms.
## Write down the sum formula and substitute
S_{n} &= \frac{a\left(1 - r^{n}\right)}{1 - r}
S_{10} &= \frac{15\left(1 - 0.6^{10}\right)}{1 - 0.6}
&= \frac{15\left(1 - 0.6^{10}\right)}{0.4}
&= 37.5\left(1 - 0.6^{10}\right)
## Evaluate
&= 37.2733\ldots
&\approx 37.27
ANSWER: 37.27 \text{ mg}

## Use the sum to infinity formula
This applies because $|r| = 0.6 < 1$, with $a = 15$.
S_{\infty} &= \frac{a}{1 - r}
&= \frac{15}{1 - 0.6}
&= \frac{15}{0.4}
&= 37.5
ANSWER: 37.5 \text{ mg}

## Write the amounts from each injection
A 15% decrease each day means each amount is multiplied by $0.85$.
Just after the $n$th injection: $d$ from the newest, $0.85d$ from the one before, and so on back to the first.
S_{n} &= d + d(0.85) + d(0.85)^2 + \dots + d(0.85)^{n-1}
## Identify the geometric series
First term $a = d$, common ratio $r = 0.85$, and $n$ terms.
S_{n} &= \frac{a\left(1 - r^{n}\right)}{1 - r}
## Substitute a = d and r = 0.85
&= \frac{d\left(1 - 0.85^{n}\right)}{1 - 0.85}
&= \frac{d\left(1 - 0.85^{n}\right)}{0.15}
## Simplify the fraction
&= \frac{100}{15}\,d\left(1 - 0.85^{n}\right)
&= \frac{20}{3}\,d\left(1 - 0.85^{n}\right)
&= \frac{20d\left(1 - 0.85^{n}\right)}{3}
ANSWER: S_n = \frac{20d\left(1 - 0.85^{n}\right)}{3}

## Differentiate P(t)
The derivative of $\ln(t+1)$ is $\frac{1}{t+1}$, and the constant $0.82$ differentiates to $0$.
P(t) &= 0.82 - 0.12\ln(t+1)
P'(t) &= -0.12 \times \frac{1}{t+1}
&= \frac{-0.12}{t+1}
## Substitute t = 1 into P'(t)
P'(1) &= \frac{-0.12}{1+1}
&= \frac{-0.12}{2}
&= -0.06
## Interpret the sign of P'(t) in part (ii)
$P'(t)$ is the rate of change of the proportion recalled. It is negative, so $P$ is decreasing.
The proportion of digits recalled correctly decreases as the time $t$ increases.
ANSWER: P'(1) = -0.06;\ \text{the proportion recalled decreases over time}

## Probability the second and third match the first
The first person can be born on any day, probability $\frac{7}{7}$.
Each of the other two must match that day, probability $\frac{1}{7}$ each.
## Multiply the probabilities
P(\text{same day}) &= \frac{7}{7} \times \frac{1}{7} \times \frac{1}{7}
&= \frac{1}{49}
ANSWER: \frac{1}{49}

## Write the section formula
Dividing $[AB]$ in the ratio $4:1$ gives $C = \frac{1\cdot A + 4\cdot B}{4+1}$ (the 1 goes with $A$, the 4 with $B$).
## Find the x-coordinate
x_C &= \frac{1(8) + 4(-1)}{4+1}
&= \frac{8 - 4}{5}
&= \frac{4}{5}
## Find the y-coordinate
y_C &= \frac{1(-4) + 4(3)}{4+1}
&= \frac{-4 + 12}{5}
&= \frac{8}{5}
## State the point
$C = \left(\frac{4}{5}, \frac{8}{5}\right)$.
ANSWER: C = \left(\frac{4}{5}, \frac{8}{5}\right)

## Write the angle formula
The angle $\theta$ between lines with slopes $m_1$ and $m_2$ satisfies $\tan\theta = \frac{m_1 - m_2}{1 + m_1 m_2}$.
Let $m_1 = -2$, $m_2 = m$ (the slope of $j$) and $\theta = 30^\circ$.
## Substitute the values
\tan 30^\circ &= \frac{-2 - m}{1 + (-2)m}
\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} &= \frac{-2 - m}{1 - 2m}
## Clear the fraction
Multiply both sides by $\sqrt{3}(1-2m)$.
1 - 2m &= \sqrt{3}(-2 - m)
1 - 2m &= -2\sqrt{3} - \sqrt{3}m
## Collect the m terms
Add $2\sqrt{3}$ and $2m$ to both sides.
1 + 2\sqrt{3} &= 2m - \sqrt{3}m
1 + 2\sqrt{3} &= m(2 - \sqrt{3})
m &= \frac{1 + 2\sqrt{3}}{2 - \sqrt{3}}
## Rationalise the denominator
Multiply top and bottom by $2 + \sqrt{3}$.
m &= \frac{(1 + 2\sqrt{3})(2 + \sqrt{3})}{(2 - \sqrt{3})(2 + \sqrt{3})}
&= \frac{2 + \sqrt{3} + 4\sqrt{3} + 6}{4 - 3}
&= \frac{8 + 5\sqrt{3}}{1}
&= 8 + 5\sqrt{3}
ANSWER: 8 + 5\sqrt{3}

## Write $A-B$ as a sum
\tan(A-B) &= \tan\bigl(A + (-B)\bigr)
## Apply the formula for $\tan(A+B)$
Use $\tan(A+B) = \dfrac{\tan A + \tan B}{1 - \tan A \tan B}$ with $B$ replaced by $-B$.
&= \frac{\tan A + \tan(-B)}{1 - \tan A\,\tan(-B)}
## Use $\tan(-B) = -\tan B$
&= \frac{\tan A - \tan B}{1 - \tan A\,(-\tan B)}
&= \frac{\tan A - \tan B}{1 + \tan A\,\tan B}
ANSWER: \tan(A-B) = \dfrac{\tan A - \tan B}{1 + \tan A \tan B}

## Write $15^\circ$ as a difference of known angles
\tan 15^\circ &= \tan(60^\circ - 45^\circ)
## Use the formula from part (i)
&= \frac{\tan 60^\circ - \tan 45^\circ}{1 + \tan 60^\circ \tan 45^\circ}
## Substitute the exact values
$\tan 60^\circ = \sqrt{3}$ and $\tan 45^\circ = 1$.
&= \frac{\sqrt{3} - 1}{1 + \sqrt{3}\times 1}
&= \frac{\sqrt{3} - 1}{\sqrt{3} + 1}
## Read off $a$
This is the required form with $a = 3$.
ANSWER: \tan 15^\circ = \dfrac{\sqrt{3}-1}{\sqrt{3}+1}
